governor asks: What should "easier to read" mean for the output? Right now `todo list` prints lines like `[ ] buy milk` and `[x] walk dog`. Which of these do you want (pick any)?
(a) Show each todo's id, e.g. `#1 [ ] buy milk`, so you can see what to pass to `complete`.
(b) Show the due date when there is one, e.g. `[ ] buy milk (due 2026-11-01)`.
(c) Line up the columns (id, status, title, due) in a table.
(d) Put open todos first, or sort them by due date.
(e) Add a summary line, e.g. `2 open, 1 done`.
(f) Something else, such as colours or changing the "Added #1" / "Completed #2" messages?
If you have an exact example of the output you want, please paste it.

